{"title":"Career Roadmap · Financial Planner","role":"Financial Planner","summary":"A Financial Planner helps individuals and families organise their finances around specific life goals and long-term financial needs.","facts":{"Current degree":"BBA / BMS / BBM","Course":"BBA – Finance"},"about":[{"label":"Degree–Career Alignment","text":"Strong"},{"label":"Primary Domains","text":"Personal Finance, Financial Planning, Investments, Insurance, Tax Planning, Retirement Planning"},{"label":"Typical Entry Level","text":"Financial Planning Associate / Wealth Management Associate / Investment Planning Associate"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"What does a Financial Planner do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Financial Planner helps individuals and families organise their finances around specific life goals and long-term financial needs."},{"type":"p","text":"The work can involve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Understanding income, expenses and liabilities"},{"text":"Identifying financial goals"},{"text":"Assessing risk tolerance and financial capacity"},{"text":"Preparing financial plans"},{"text":"Asset-allocation analysis"},{"text":"Investment planning"},{"text":"Insurance planning"},{"text":"Retirement planning"},{"text":"Tax-planning coordination"},{"text":"Education and other goal planning"},{"text":"Portfolio reviews"},{"text":"Cash-flow planning"},{"text":"Monitoring progress toward financial goals"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important distinction","text":"Financial planning, investment distribution and regulated investment advice are not necessarily the same activity. In India, the permissions and regulatory requirements depend on the services being provided. A BBA Finance degree alone does not automatically authorise someone to provide regulated investment advice."}]},{"heading":"Career Development Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Approx. Timeline","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Finance + accounting"}],[{"text":"Investment foundation"},{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Markets + products"}],[{"text":"Planning skills"},{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Financial planning"}],[{"text":"Industry readiness"},{"text":"Year 3–4"},{"text":"Internship + certification"}],[{"text":"First job"},{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Planning/wealth associate"}],[{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Financial planning / wealth management"}],[{"text":"Senior level"},{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Planner / Wealth Manager"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"8–15+ years"},{"text":"Financial Planning Head / Practice Owner"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Build the Finance Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Financial Accounting"},{"text":"Business Economics"},{"text":"Business Mathematics"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Financial Management"},{"text":"Business Law"},{"text":"Corporate Finance fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Personal finance fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Income"},{"text":"Expenses"},{"text":"Savings"},{"text":"Emergency funds"},{"text":"Debt"},{"text":"Interest rates"},{"text":"Inflation"},{"text":"Time value of money"},{"text":"Compounding"},{"text":"Cash flow"},{"text":"Net worth"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A good planner must understand the entire financial position of a client, not just investments."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Investments & Financial Products"},{"type":"p","text":"Build broad product knowledge."},{"type":"h","text":"Investments"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Equity"},{"text":"Bonds"},{"text":"Fixed deposits"},{"text":"Mutual funds"},{"text":"ETFs"},{"text":"Government securities"},{"text":"Pension products"},{"text":"Gold"},{"text":"REITs/InvITs"},{"text":"Alternative investments at a conceptual level"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mutual funds"},{"typ